Pat Rankin <nethack.rankin@eql.caltech.edu> says:

>      Or play in color; tame monsters will be displayed in white instead of
> the "normal" color for that particular critter.  Users with color hardware
> have a definite advantage over those with monochrome displays.

You could always use the slash key.  Pressing "/" will allow you to point
at something with the cursor, and the game will tell you what it is.
This works for both monsters and things laying on the floor.
Color makes it better because you don't have to press "/" all the time,
but it is still useful.  There are so many different monsters that some
both have the same letter and color.
I once ran into a balchiterium thinking it was a rothe...
